ll_id": "toolu_01Qqf4P4Z5Zzhhz9MU2QbHXB", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconciled_executed", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 61290, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Qqf4P4Z5Zzhhz9MU2QbHXB", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 68967, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened a SEV2 incident, which paged on-call.\n\n- **What was wrong:** v2.3.1 was live in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with an 18% error rate. Its release candidate, v2.3.1-rc, was also marked unhealthy.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release marked healthy. All three regions are now running it, it reports healthy, and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2) says what failed, which version we rolled back to, and that the service has recovered. It also says the cause of the v2.3.1 failure needs to be found before anyone redeploys it.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01N1Ar9kALi5Zn6vjeWJLDvE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01FNtogacfFSqJscW7VG7VqR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01U9apfUVg3p85fS8KL9P6CM", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.92}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01XgbU7kpCbRu4vy94jV73fL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Qqf4P4Z5Zzhhz9MU2QbHXB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the latest deploy, checkout-api v2.3.1 was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of 18%. v2.3.1-rc was also marked unhealthy. checkout-api was rolled back in all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. After the rollback, the service reports healthy on v2.3.0 in all regions with an error rate of 0.2%. Next step: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened a SEV2 incident, which paged on-call.\n\n- **What was wrong:** v2.3.1 was live in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with an 18% error rate. Its release candidate, v2.3.1-rc, was also marked unhealthy.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release marked healthy. All three regions are now running it, it reports healthy, and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2) says what failed, which version we rolled back to, and that the service has recovered. It also says the cause of the v2.3.1 failure needs to be found before anyone redeploys it.", "type": "text"}]}]}